    "upstreamCase": "Designate G1 + LS1; Designate G2 + LS2; Designate G3 + LS3",
    "license": "MIT",
    "licenseNotice": "LICENSE.libvterm.txt",
    "recordedDeviations": [
      "DanTerm prints two-character GL runs where upstream prints one, so each invocation also crosses the bulk print path.",
      "The closing SO is DanTerm's addition: it re-invokes G1 after G2 and G3 were designated, which upstream never re-reads a slot it left behind.",
      "Upstream also reaches G2 and G3 through the 8-bit single shifts 0x8e and 0x8f; DanTerm has no 8-bit C1 path, and TerminalCharsetTests pins the 7-bit ESC N and ESC O forms instead."
    ]
  },
